1. `paper.tex` loads `\usepackage{neurips_2026}` with no `final`/`preprint` option.
2. `neurips_2026.sty` in the delivery is byte-identical to `template/neurips_2026.sty`.
3. `paper.pdf` compiles from the delivered sources with `pdflatex` (TeX Live 2026 provided),
   US Letter, no Type 3 fonts, pages numbered.
4. Content pages (through the end of the main text, excluding references, appendices,
   checklist) number at most 9.
5. `checklist.tex` has no `\answerTODO` and no instruction block; questions unmodified.
6. Nothing identifying anywhere in `paper.tex`, `code/`, `results/`.
7. `code/` and `results/` are nonempty, with a README and provenance (which inputs produced
   which results).
